// A large component, so `crate`'s chunk is at the 16 KiB target: a row of 196 bytes (48 floats and the list's `int32`
// length) and its 8-byte handle gives 80 rows of 204 bytes, 16,320 bytes. The world builds such a chunk in its table's
// block; the 32 KiB frame guard holds it off the stack on wasm. A bounded list is one size on every target since kama
// 0.9.896 (KY-47), so the row count is too.

import { std::collections::InlineDynamicArray };

export { Bulk };

@generate(Serializable, Deserializable)
type value Bulk { @field public InlineDynamicArray<float32>#(48) xs = InlineDynamicArray.empty(); public default ctor make() { } }
